that I had to make some friends,

00:11:48.667 --> 00:11:50.968
so Henry told me to make some friends,

00:11:50.968 --> 00:11:53.467
and I did it the best I knew how.

00:11:53.467 --> 00:11:54.808
- How?

00:11:54.808 --> 00:11:55.866
- I put up some fliers.

00:11:55.866 --> 00:11:56.463
- What?!

00:11:56.463 --> 00:11:57.842
(all laugh)

00:12:00.882 --> 00:12:02.682
(jazzy music)

00:12:08.943 --> 00:12:11.004
- [Colin] My mom didn't
like this idea very much.

00:12:11.004 --> 00:12:13.343
She said it seemed kinda dangerous,

00:12:13.343 --> 00:12:14.783
but it only took about 20 minutes

00:12:14.783 --> 00:12:17.582
before I started meeting
other people on the street,

00:12:17.582 --> 00:12:20.241
and of course they were
making a video too.

00:12:26.268 --> 00:12:27.174
- [Voiceover] I'm Jenny.

00:12:27.174 --> 00:12:28.754
- Let's break the wall.

00:12:28.754 --> 00:12:30.205
- Hey!

00:12:30.943 --> 00:12:32.023
- [Colin] So I followed these two guys

00:12:32.023 --> 00:12:34.023
around the corner to a building

00:12:34.023 --> 00:12:37.364
that I actually thought was
abandoned, and it's not,

00:12:37.364 --> 00:12:39.423
but, well I guess that
kinda sounds sketchy

00:12:39.423 --> 00:12:41.162
now that I say it out loud.

00:12:41.503 --> 00:12:43.383
(peppy music)

00:12:47.404 --> 00:12:49.644
This is insane.

00:12:56.319 --> 00:12:58.281
- [Voiceover] That is a weird shout.

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:00.740
- [Guy in Grey] Just gonna play it out

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:01.456
like it was all planned.

00:13:01.456 --> 00:13:04.755
Actually, Buzzfeed came in
today to jump with Ryan.

00:13:07.715 --> 00:13:12.715
- Our studio, it's always
been a lot of local people.

00:13:14.553 --> 00:13:15.513
- [Colin] I was feeling pretty confident

00:13:15.513 --> 00:13:16.673
in my plan at this point.

00:13:16.673 --> 00:13:17.934
I mean, I didn't really do anything,

00:13:17.934 --> 00:13:20.753
and I was already getting
tours of big, cool art studios,

00:13:20.753 --> 00:13:22.334
and jumping on trampolines.

00:13:22.334 --> 00:13:23.273
- Alright guys, cool, thanks.

00:13:23.273 --> 00:13:24.254
Nice to meet you.

00:13:24.254 --> 00:13:25.534
- And you found me on Instagram?

00:13:25.534 --> 00:13:28.033
- Yeah, I'll put it on for
you, write a little thing.

00:13:30.193 --> 00:13:33.932
- Alright, to the lake.

00:13:34.089 --> 00:13:36.169
(peppy music)

00:13:47.648 --> 00:13:48.366
- Wave, Jenny.

00:13:48.366 --> 00:13:50.686
I started getting a little
cocky with my skills.

00:13:50.686 --> 00:13:52.985
I'm gonna introduce myself
to this gentleman over here.

00:14:04.701 --> 00:14:05.879
- [Colin] Hey, this is Andrew.

00:14:05.879 --> 00:14:07.290
- Hey, people.

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:09.207
- We met Andrew while
he was eating breakfast.

00:14:09.207 --> 00:14:10.207
- Yeah.

00:14:10.207 --> 00:14:11.949
- 'Cause he was getting
a late start today.

00:14:11.949 --> 00:14:12.469
- Yeah.

00:14:12.469 --> 00:14:13.970
- There's probably like people
sitting around everywhere

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:14.930
who are like, aw man,

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:16.610
I wish had more people to
hang out with on Friday.

00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:17.530
- Right, you know,

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:19.789
who are thinking the same thing
and wanting the same thing.

00:14:19.789 --> 00:14:21.210
Really, I think it's,
you have to be sort of

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:24.636
open in your possibilities,
as cliche as that sounds.

00:14:24.636 --> 00:14:25.978
I've only been out here for an hour,

00:14:25.978 --> 00:14:28.127
and I feel like I'm gonna get heat stroke.

00:14:28.127 --> 00:14:29.908
Andrew and I had a lovely afternoon,

00:14:29.908 --> 00:14:32.028
and I went home thinking my day was over,

00:14:32.028 --> 00:14:33.487
but when I checked my e-mail,

00:14:33.487 --> 00:14:36.695
I discovered that my fliers
were actually working.

00:14:38.827 --> 00:14:39.508
I'm trying to pick out a beer,

00:14:39.508 --> 00:14:41.837
'cause I got invited to a potluck tonight.

00:14:45.936 --> 00:14:46.695
- Hello?

00:14:46.695 --> 00:14:47.328
- [Colin] Hey!

00:14:47.328 --> 00:14:49.128
- Colin, get up here, man!

00:14:49.128 --> 00:14:49.697
Nice to to meet you!

00:14:49.697 --> 00:14:51.116
- [Colin] Nice to meet you too.

00:14:51.116 --> 00:14:51.795
That's JP.

00:14:51.795 --> 00:14:53.177
He saw one of my fliers by the lake.

00:14:53.177 --> 00:14:54.156
- How are ya? Come on in!

00:14:54.156 --> 00:14:54.746
- [Colin] Thanks!

00:14:54.746 --> 00:14:57.757
- [Voiceover] Did you guys,
how do you all know each other?

00:14:59.237 --> 00:15:01.845
- We're gonna have pulled
pork sandwiches, guys.

00:15:05.224 --> 00:15:07.403
Ah! No!

00:15:08.464 --> 00:15:10.483
Just bros, meat, and video games.

00:15:10.483 --> 00:15:13.544
I totally forgot how much
I miss this kind of thing.

00:15:13.544 --> 00:15:15.045
- Donkey Kong's slow, right?

00:15:15.045 --> 00:15:17.424
- Yeah, but he does hit hard.

00:15:19.125 --> 00:15:20.143
- Dang it!

00:15:20.143 --> 00:15:21.322
I lost a second befo--

00:15:21.322 --> 00:15:23.162
Well, I'm first out.

00:15:26.103 --> 00:15:28.223
- I think that's her.

00:15:36.983 --> 00:15:38.383
Sophie?

00:15:39.063 --> 00:15:41.583
- Oh yes, hello, hi.

00:15:41.583 --> 00:15:43.722
- [Colin] It's pretty bold for
a woman to call on a flier,

00:15:43.722 --> 00:15:47.442
but after a couple beers and a few tacos,

00:15:47.442 --> 00:15:49.202
we both got a little more
comfortable with each other,

00:15:49.202 --> 00:15:51.482
and started talking a bit about friendship

00:15:51.482 --> 00:15:53.359
and what it really means.

00:15:53.359 --> 00:15:54.663
And then, when we got on the subject

00:15:54.663 --> 00:15:57.382
of making friends as an adult,

00:15:57.382 --> 00:15:59.902
she said something that
really struck a chord with me,

00:15:59.902 --> 00:16:02.060
and I haven't really forgotten about it.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.222
- I guess the hardest
part about making friends

00:16:04.222 --> 00:16:08.022
is admitting that you
want to make new friends,

00:16:08.022 --> 00:16:10.441
because you feel like
when you're an adult,

00:16:10.441 --> 00:16:12.302
you should already have friends,

00:16:12.302 --> 00:16:14.622
and you should have already
found your place in the world,

00:16:14.622 --> 00:16:15.841
but really, you like,

00:16:15.841 --> 00:16:19.521
don't know what's going on
at all, and that's okay.

00:16:19.521 --> 00:16:20.462
- [Colin] Right there.

00:16:20.462 --> 00:16:22.382
That's when she nailed
it, and she's right.

00:16:22.382 --> 00:16:23.622
The only thing that really gets in the way

00:16:23.622 --> 00:16:25.262
of making new friends is ego.

00:16:25.262 --> 00:16:29.081
I mean, nobody really has
this shit figured out.

00:16:29.081 --> 00:16:30.481
So, I decided to start calling back

00:16:30.481 --> 00:16:32.001
the new friends I've made,

00:16:32.001 --> 00:16:33.062
because I realized that that

00:16:33.062 --> 00:16:36.158
was a lot scarier than meeting new people.

00:16:36.158 --> 00:16:38.040
Meeting new friends was
starting to feel easy,

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:39.640
and that's when I got a call from Jessie,

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:40.720
an Echo Park native who was

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:43.741
looking for a sofa on Craig's
List, and found me instead.

00:16:43.741 --> 00:16:46.541
After a few tacos, we
hit it off immediately.

00:16:46.541 --> 00:16:48.981
- If I need it, I'll get
a haircut right there,

00:16:48.981 --> 00:16:49.531
Casanova's number two.

00:16:49.531 --> 00:16:50.470
- That's where you go?

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:51.630
- Yeah.

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:52.770
- [Colin] I learned something important

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:54.231
from all my new friends.

00:16:54.231 --> 00:16:55.770
I realized that it's just not that weird

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:57.871
to call a friendly-looking
dude on a flier.

00:16:57.871 --> 00:17:00.170
It pays to just put yourself out there,

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:01.951
and, you know, make the connection.

00:17:01.951 --> 00:17:04.850
- You're just talking
because I drive a moped.

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:05.680
- [Colin] And yeah...

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:07.062
- 'Cause I drive a moped.

00:17:07.062 --> 00:17:09.092
- [Colin] New friends have perks.

00:17:10.242 --> 00:17:12.562
(victorious music)

00:17:19.222 --> 00:17:21.243
(smooth music)

00:17:25.582 --> 00:17:26.923
- Alright, so, speaking of friends,

00:17:26.923 --> 00:17:29.243
are you ready to watch one
of your oldest friends?

00:17:29.243 --> 00:17:30.403
- [Ella] Julia's known me through

00:17:30.403 --> 00:17:32.043
different periods of my life.

00:17:32.043 --> 00:17:33.281
- [Henry] She's known you
the longest of these three.

00:17:33.281 --> 00:17:34.961
- [Ella] Yeah, so, it'll
be interesting to see

00:17:34.961 --> 00:17:37.963
if she has a similar view of me.

00:17:37.963 --> 00:17:39.782
- I met Ella in seventh grade.

00:17:39.782 --> 00:17:41.502
I don't remember my first impression.

00:17:41.502 --> 00:17:42.542
She was kind of quiet,

00:17:42.542 --> 00:17:44.321
kind of like the weird girl in the corner.

00:17:44.321 --> 00:17:45.462
- [Henry] She was a
weird girl in the corner.

00:17:45.462 --> 00:17:46.942
- Yeah, but I kind of was too,

00:17:46.942 --> 00:17:48.953
so I think that's why we clicked.

00:17:50.433 --> 00:17:52.892
- Why am I the quiet, weird one?

00:17:52.892 --> 00:17:55.913
- I think one of my first
memories of her is in school.

00:17:55.913 --> 00:17:59.873
We were playing with large water bottles.

00:17:59.873 --> 00:18:01.812
- Of course she's gonna tell this story.

00:18:01.812 --> 00:18:04.332
This is, I think about this a lot.

00:18:04.332 --> 00:18:06.772
It's when I smacked her
in the face with a bottle

00:18:06.772 --> 00:18:08.952
and she started crying, right?

00:18:08.952 --> 00:18:11.264
- A water jug, exactly, and she ended up

00:18:11.264 --> 00:18:13.191
smashing me in the face with one of them.

00:18:13.191 --> 00:18:14.991
So, that was like my
first real memory of Ella,

00:18:14.991 --> 00:18:17.092
was me being in pain.

00:18:17.092 --> 00:18:18.791
- Of course she tells that story.

00:18:18.791 --> 00:18:21.111
I remember just being like, well,

00:18:21.111 --> 00:18:22.311
never gonna have friends again,

00:18:22.311 --> 00:18:24.172
'cause my new friend is crying now

00:18:24.172 --> 00:18:26.012
and she'll hate me forever.

00:18:26.012 --> 00:18:28.932
- [Henry] What do you like
about Ella, as a person?

00:18:28.932 --> 00:18:33.273
- The first thing that came to
my mind is her impulsiveness.

00:18:33.273 --> 00:18:34.753
She just decides she
wants to do something,

00:18:34.753 --> 00:18:36.590
she doesn't over-think
it, and she does it.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.240
- I wanna note that this is, I think,

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:41.040
the third person who has
called you impulsive.

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:43.902
- Yeah, I never thought that about myself.

00:18:43.902 --> 00:18:46.600
- [Henry] What does your
friendship look like in 20 years?

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.822
- We're gonna be friends forever.

00:18:48.822 --> 00:18:51.600
Yeah, whether that's
long-distance friendship,

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:53.259
like we've done in the past.

00:18:53.259 --> 00:18:54.800
I still have a friend crush on her.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:55.532
- You still have a friend crush on her?

00:18:55.532 --> 00:18:57.525
- Yeah, I still wanna be her friend.

00:18:59.085 --> 00:19:00.925
(groovy music)

00:19:05.261 --> 00:19:07.343
- Do you feel closer to your friends now,

00:19:07.343 --> 00:19:08.565
that we did this with?

00:19:08.565 --> 00:19:12.423
- [Ella] I feel like I,
weirdly know more about myself,

00:19:12.423 --> 00:19:14.463
just from what they were saying.

00:19:14.463 --> 00:19:16.223
It's amazing to hear that

00:19:16.223 --> 00:19:19.782
they really do like me for who I am,

00:19:19.782 --> 00:19:21.841
and want to be friends with me.

00:19:21.841 --> 00:19:24.982
- Remember that friendship is a process,

00:19:24.982 --> 00:19:28.102
and you'll be better if you're
like, intentional about it,

00:19:28.102 --> 00:19:29.942
and actually think about your friends,

00:19:29.942 --> 00:19:31.902
as opposed to just like
going through life,

00:19:31.902 --> 00:19:34.022
taking friendship for granted,

00:19:34.022 --> 00:19:35.524
kids.

00:19:35.524 --> 00:19:36.284
- Babes.

00:19:36.284 --> 00:19:37.062
- Babes.

00:19:37.062 --> 00:19:38.001
- Bros.

00:19:38.001 --> 00:19:39.484
- [Henry] Pretty good way to wrap it up.

00:19:39.484 --> 00:19:40.902
Thank you guys for watching.

00:19:40.902 --> 00:19:42.404
What it do?

00:19:42.404 --> 00:19:43.795
- What it do?!

00:19:43.795 --> 00:19:45.035
- What it do.

00:19:45.035 --> 00:19:46.315
- [Henry] This episode of
Real Mature was produced

00:19:46.315 --> 00:19:47.995
by the BuzzFeedIRL team,

00:19:47.995 --> 00:19:51.195
including me, Ryan B,
Colin, Abe, and Michelle.

00:19:51.195 --> 00:19:54.195
Thanks to birocratic, CMA
Music, and Nkato for the beats,

00:19:54.195 --> 00:19:57.725
Jesse for the graphic help,
and everyone who in the video.

00:19:57.725 --> 00:19:59.381
(cool music)

